Drafting a conceptual pseudocode simulation to validate:

Initialize platform = [1,2,3]; ramp = [4..100]
repeat until all 100 processed:
  choose random piston in {1,2,3}
  if piston == 1:
    eject platform[1]; shift platform[2]->1, platform[3]->2; load next ramp ball to 3
  if piston == 2:
    eject platform[2]; release platform[1]; move platform[3]->1; load next two ramp balls to 2 and 3
  if piston == 3:
    eject platform[3]; release platform[1]; move platform[2]->1; load next two ramp balls to 2 and 3
Track for each ball whether it was ejected by a piston vs released.
Run many trials; estimate ejection probabilities.
Heuristic expectation based on the logic: ball 3 > ball 2 > ball 1 for initial triple. The simulation should confirm ball 3 as best choice.
